# Known-accepted findings, not app-level vulnerabilities:

# All 5 CVEs below are in golang.org/x/net inside usr/bin/pebble, a service-manager binary
# bundled by the eclipse-temurin:21-jre base image (docs/devops-shams-ma.md's approved base
# image). Our app never invokes pebble (entrypoint is `java -jar app.jar` directly), so these
# are not part of the app's actual attack surface. Revisit if Eclipse Temurin ships a rebuilt
# image with a patched pebble, or if the base image choice changes.
CVE-2026-25681
CVE-2026-27136
CVE-2026-33814
CVE-2026-39821
CVE-2026-39822

# GHSA-qwww-vcr4-c8h2 (react-router, fixed in 8.3.0): CSRF bypass specific to React Router's RSC
# (React Server Components) framework mode — action execution before the expected 400 response.
# This app is a plain client-side SPA (frontend/src/App.tsx: declarative <Routes>/<Route>, no
# data router, no loaders/actions, no RSC), so the vulnerable code path is never reached. A fix
# requires a react-router-dom 7->8 major bump; revisit when that's done for other reasons rather
# than rushing a major-version jump under a security-gate deadline.
GHSA-qwww-vcr4-c8h2
